    {
      "@id": "concept:human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017-sch-2-sec-10",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "10 At the end of section 20",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017#sch-2-sec-10"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017.pdf, p.7",
      "values:originalText": "Add:\n\n(9) The Commission must act fairly in the performance of the\nfunctions referred to in paragraph 11(1)(f).\n\n(10) If a complaint is made under paragraph (1)(b), the Commission:\n\n(a) must act expeditiously in dealing with the complaint; and\n\nSchedule 2  Amendment of the Australian Human Rights Commission Act 1986\n\nHuman Rights Legislation Amendment Act 2017\n\nCompilation date: 01/09/2021\nRegistered: 03/11/2021\n\n(b) must use the Commission’s best endeavours to finish dealing\nwith the complaint within 12 months after the complaint was\nmade.\n\n(11) Subsections (9) and (10) do not impose a duty on the Commission\nthat is enforceable in court.\n\n(12) Subsection (11) does not affect a legally enforceable obligation to\nobserve the rules of natural justice.",
      "skos:definition": "Add:\n\n(9) The Commission must act fairly in the performance of the\nfunctions referred to in paragraph 11(1)(f).\n\n(10) If a complaint is made under paragraph (1)(b), the Commission:\n\n(a) must act expeditiously in dealing with the complaint; and\n\nSchedule 2  Amendment of the Australian Human Rights Commission Act 1986\n\nHuman Rights Legislation Amendment Act 2017\n\nCompilation date: 01/09/2021\nRegistered: 03/11/2021\n\n(b) must use the Commission’s best endeavours to finish dealing\nwith the complaint within 12 months after the complaint was\nmade.\n\n(11) Subsections (9) and (10) do not impose a duty on the Commission\nthat is enforceable in court.\n\n(12) Subsection (11) does not affect a legally enforceable obligation to\nobserve the rules of natural justice.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017-sch-2-sec-10-ss-9"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017-sch-2-sec-10-ss-10"
        },
