    {
      "@id": "concept:human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017-sch-2-sec-15",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15 At the end of section 32",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017#sch-2-sec-15"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017.pdf, p.9",
      "values:originalText": "Add:\n\n(4) The Commission must act fairly in the performance of the\nfunctions referred to in paragraph 31(b).\n\n(5) If a complaint is made under paragraph (1)(b), the Commission:\n\n(a) must act expeditiously in dealing with the complaint; and\n\n(b) must use the Commission’s best endeavours to finish dealing\nwith the complaint within 12 months after the complaint was\nmade.\n\n(6) Subsections (4) and (5) do not impose a duty on the Commission\nthat is enforceable in court.\n\n(7) Subsection (6) does not affect a legally enforceable obligation to\nobserve the rules of natural justice.",
      "skos:definition": "Add:\n\n(4) The Commission must act fairly in the performance of the\nfunctions referred to in paragraph 31(b).\n\n(5) If a complaint is made under paragraph (1)(b), the Commission:\n\n(a) must act expeditiously in dealing with the complaint; and\n\n(b) must use the Commission’s best endeavours to finish dealing\nwith the complaint within 12 months after the complaint was\nmade.\n\n(6) Subsections (4) and (5) do not impose a duty on the Commission\nthat is enforceable in court.\n\n(7) Subsection (6) does not affect a legally enforceable obligation to\nobserve the rules of natural justice.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017-sch-2-sec-15-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017-sch-2-sec-15-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017-sch-2-sec-15-ss-6"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017-sch-2-sec-15-ss-7"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f552a1e79bdc74d313b3f0f000e309faa363c9b81f8db6b9d0fb2b41f0dcea48"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017#sch-2-sec-15",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15 At the end of section 32",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 9,
      "values:originalText": "Add:\n\n(4) The Commission must act fairly in the performance of the\nfunctions referred to in paragraph 31(b).\n\n(5) If a complaint is made under paragraph (1)(b), the Commission:\n\n(a) must act expeditiously in dealing with the complaint; and\n\n(b) must use the Commission’s best endeavours to finish dealing\nwith the complaint within 12 months after the complaint was\nmade.\n\n(6) Subsections (4) and (5) do not impose a duty on the Commission\nthat is enforceable in court.\n\n(7) Subsection (6) does not affect a legally enforceable obligation to\nobserve the rules of natural justice."
    },
    {
