    {
      "@id": "concept:human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017-sch-2-sec-31",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "31 Subsection 46PF(1)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017#sch-2-sec-31"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017.pdf, p.12",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(1) Subject to subsections (1A) and (5), if a complaint is referred to the\nPresident under section 46PD, the President must:\n\n(a) consider whether to inquire into the complaint, having regard\nto the matters referred to in section 46PH; and\n\n(b) if the President is of the opinion that the complaint should be\nterminated—terminate the complaint without inquiry; and\n\n(c) unless the President terminates the complaint under\nparagraph (b) or section 46PH—inquire into the complaint\nand attempt to conciliate the complaint.\n\n(1A) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(a), the President may inform\nhimself or herself of such facts and circumstances as are necessary\nto form the opinion referred to in paragraph (1)(b).\n\n(1B) If the President terminates the complaint under paragraph (1)(b),\nthe President must comply with the notification requirements of\nsubsections 46PH(2), (2A) and (3).",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(1) Subject to subsections (1A) and (5), if a complaint is referred to the\nPresident under section 46PD, the President must:\n\n(a) consider whether to inquire into the complaint, having regard\nto the matters referred to in section 46PH; and\n\n(b) if the President is of the opinion that the complaint should be\nterminated—terminate the complaint without inquiry; and\n\n(c) unless the President terminates the complaint under\nparagraph (b) or section 46PH—inquire into the complaint\nand attempt to conciliate the complaint.\n\n(1A) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(a), the President may inform\nhimself or herself of such facts and circumstances as are necessary\nto form the opinion referred to in paragraph (1)(b).\n\n(1B) If the President terminates the complaint under paragraph (1)(b),\nthe President must comply with the notification requirements of\nsubsections 46PH(2), (2A) and (3).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017-sch-2-sec-31-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017-sch-2-sec-31-ss-1a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017-sch-2-sec-31-ss-1b"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "fc61fc4a50e655d12b70c909f99174b3a8932dca19bfcf9d8128e3cad72db45b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017#sch-2-sec-31",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "31 Subsection 46PF(1)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 12,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(1) Subject to subsections (1A) and (5), if a complaint is referred to the\nPresident under section 46PD, the President must:\n\n(a) consider whether to inquire into the complaint, having regard\nto the matters referred to in section 46PH; and\n\n(b) if the President is of the opinion that the complaint should be\nterminated—terminate the complaint without inquiry; and\n\n(c) unless the President terminates the complaint under\nparagraph (b) or section 46PH—inquire into the complaint\nand attempt to conciliate the complaint.\n\n(1A) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(a), the President may inform\nhimself or herself of such facts and circumstances as are necessary\nto form the opinion referred to in paragraph (1)(b).\n\n(1B) If the President terminates the complaint under paragraph (1)(b),\nthe President must comply with the notification requirements of\nsubsections 46PH(2), (2A) and (3)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017-sch-2-sec-31-ss-1",
