      },
      "dc:source": "human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017.pdf, p.13",
      "values:originalText": "(7) If the President has decided to inquire into a complaint, the\nPresident:\n\n(a) must notify the complaint to the respondent, unless the\nPresident is satisfied that notification would be likely to\nprejudice the safety of a person; and\n\n(b) if the complaint is amended under subsection (3) by adding a\nrespondent—must notify the complaint to that respondent,\nunless the President is satisfied that notification would be\nlikely to prejudice the safety of a person; and\n\n(c) if any person (other than the respondent) is the subject of an\nadverse allegation arising from the complaint—must notify\nthe person of the adverse allegation, unless the President is\nsatisfied:\n\n(i) that notification would be likely to prejudice the safety\nof a person; or\n\n(ii) that it is not practicable to do so; and\n\n(d) may notify the complaint to any person who, in the opinion\nof the President, is likely to be able to provide information\nrelevant to the complaint.",
      "skos:definition": "(7) If the President has decided to inquire into a complaint, the\nPresident:\n\n(a) must notify the complaint to the respondent, unless the\nPresident is satisfied that notification would be likely to\nprejudice the safety of a person; and\n\n(b) if the complaint is amended under subsection (3) by adding a\nrespondent—must notify the complaint to that respondent,\nunless the President is satisfied that notification would be\nlikely to prejudice the safety of a person; and\n\n(c) if any person (other than the respondent) is the subject of an\nadverse allegation arising from the complaint—must notify\nthe person of the adverse allegation, unless the President is\nsatisfied:\n\n(i) that notification would be likely to prejudice the safety\nof a person; or\n\n(ii) that it is not practicable to do so; and\n\n(d) may notify the complaint to any person who, in the opinion\nof the President, is likely to be able to provide information\nrelevant to the complaint.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017-sch-2-sec-36"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017-sch-2-sec-36-ss-7-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017-sch-2-sec-36-ss-7-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7b4684c86460ce3e6d9a154f7540e0c0566224f6853b7b2768da7155890247e4",
      "skos:note": "Must notify certain persons of a complaint",
      "dc:description": "Notification"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017#sch-2-sec-36-ss-7",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "36(7) At the end of section 46PF",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 13,
      "values:originalText": "(7) If the President has decided to inquire into a complaint, the\nPresident:\n\n(a) must notify the complaint to the respondent, unless the\nPresident is satisfied that notification would be likely to\nprejudice the safety of a person; and\n\n(b) if the complaint is amended under subsection (3) by adding a\nrespondent—must notify the complaint to that respondent,\nunless the President is satisfied that notification would be\nlikely to prejudice the safety of a person; and\n\n(c) if any person (other than the respondent) is the subject of an\nadverse allegation arising from the complaint—must notify\nthe person of the adverse allegation, unless the President is\nsatisfied:\n\n(i) that notification would be likely to prejudice the safety\nof a person; or\n\n(ii) that it is not practicable to do so; and\n\n(d) may notify the complaint to any person who, in the opinion\nof the President, is likely to be able to provide information\nrelevant to the complaint."
    },
