    {
      "@id": "concept:human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017-sch-2-sec-36-ss-8",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "36(8) At the end of section 46PF",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017#sch-2-sec-36-ss-8"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017.pdf, p.13",
      "values:originalText": "(8) For the purposes of paragraphs (7)(a), (b) and (c), the President\nmust notify the respondent or the other person, as the case may be:\n\nSchedule 2  Amendment of the Australian Human Rights Commission Act 1986\n\nHuman Rights Legislation Amendment Act 2017\n\nCompilation date: 01/09/2021\nRegistered: 03/11/2021\n\n(a) under paragraph (7)(a)—as soon as the President has decided\nto inquire into the complaint; or\n\n(b) under paragraph (7)(b)—as soon as the complaint has been\namended; or\n\n(c) under paragraph (7)(c)—as soon as the President forms the\nopinion that the person is the subject of an adverse allegation\narising from the complaint.",
      "skos:definition": "(8) For the purposes of paragraphs (7)(a), (b) and (c), the President\nmust notify the respondent or the other person, as the case may be:\n\nSchedule 2  Amendment of the Australian Human Rights Commission Act 1986\n\nHuman Rights Legislation Amendment Act 2017\n\nCompilation date: 01/09/2021\nRegistered: 03/11/2021\n\n(a) under paragraph (7)(a)—as soon as the President has decided\nto inquire into the complaint; or\n\n(b) under paragraph (7)(b)—as soon as the complaint has been\namended; or\n\n(c) under paragraph (7)(c)—as soon as the President forms the\nopinion that the person is the subject of an adverse allegation\narising from the complaint.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017-sch-2-sec-36"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017-sch-2-sec-36-ss-8-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017-sch-2-sec-36-ss-8-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "995900a3c3d43aea291d494a64e67b791799bd67b684ab1fd203446f1f406536",
      "skos:note": "Notify respondent or other person upon specified events"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017#sch-2-sec-36-ss-8",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "36(8) At the end of section 46PF",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 13,
      "values:originalText": "(8) For the purposes of paragraphs (7)(a), (b) and (c), the President\nmust notify the respondent or the other person, as the case may be:\n\nSchedule 2  Amendment of the Australian Human Rights Commission Act 1986\n\nHuman Rights Legislation Amendment Act 2017\n\nCompilation date: 01/09/2021\nRegistered: 03/11/2021\n\n(a) under paragraph (7)(a)—as soon as the President has decided\nto inquire into the complaint; or\n\n(b) under paragraph (7)(b)—as soon as the complaint has been\namended; or\n\n(c) under paragraph (7)(c)—as soon as the President forms the\nopinion that the person is the subject of an adverse allegation\narising from the complaint."
    },
