    {
      "@id": "concept:human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017-sch-2-sec-36-ss-9",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "36(9) At the end of section 46PF",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017#sch-2-sec-36-ss-9"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017.pdf, p.13",
      "values:originalText": "(9) For the purposes of subsections (7) and (8), adverse allegation\nmeans an allegation:\n\n(a) that:\n\n(i) one or more acts have been done; or\n\n(ii) one or more omissions or practices have occurred; and\n\n(b) that those acts, omissions or practices are unlawful\ndiscrimination.\nNote:\nUnlawful discrimination is defined in subsection 3(1).",
      "skos:definition": "(9) For the purposes of subsections (7) and (8), adverse allegation\nmeans an allegation:\n\n(a) that:\n\n(i) one or more acts have been done; or\n\n(ii) one or more omissions or practices have occurred; and\n\n(b) that those acts, omissions or practices are unlawful\ndiscrimination.\nNote:\nUnlawful discrimination is defined in subsection 3(1).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017-sch-2-sec-36"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017-sch-2-sec-36-ss-9-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017-sch-2-sec-36-ss-9-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017-sch-2-sec-36-ss-9-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "553173aa65ff5925d51aa48a375010b963c52d0969e537a5332fd6f63b3a597b",
      "skos:note": "Definition of adverse allegation for purposes of subsections (7) and (8)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017#sch-2-sec-36-ss-9",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "36(9) At the end of section 46PF",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 13,
      "values:originalText": "(9) For the purposes of subsections (7) and (8), adverse allegation\nmeans an allegation:\n\n(a) that:\n\n(i) one or more acts have been done; or\n\n(ii) one or more omissions or practices have occurred; and\n\n(b) that those acts, omissions or practices are unlawful\ndiscrimination.\nNote:\nUnlawful discrimination is defined in subsection 3(1)."
    },
