        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "An act, omission or practice may not be unlawful discrimination",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Consideration of exemption applies"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017-sch-2-sec-43",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "43 After subsection 46PH(1)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017#sch-2-sec-43"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017.pdf, p.15",
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\n(1A) A complaint may be terminated under subsection (1) at any time,\neven if an inquiry into the complaint has begun.\n\nSchedule 2  Amendment of the Australian Human Rights Commission Act 1986\n\nHuman Rights Legislation Amendment Act 2017\n\nCompilation date: 01/09/2021\nRegistered: 03/11/2021\n\nMandatory termination of complaint\n\n(1B) The President must terminate a complaint if the President is\nsatisfied that:\n\n(a) the complaint is trivial, vexatious, misconceived or lacking in\nsubstance; or\n\n(b) there is no reasonable prospect of the matter being settled by\nconciliation.\n\n(1C) The President must terminate a complaint if the President is\nsatisfied that there would be no reasonable prospect that the\nFederal Court or the Federal Circuit Court would be satisfied that\nthe alleged acts, omissions or practices are unlawful\ndiscrimination.\n\n(1D) A complaint may be terminated under subsection (1B) or (1C) at\nany time, even if an inquiry into the complaint has begun.",
      "skos:definition": "Insert:\n\n(1A) A complaint may be terminated under subsection (1) at any time,\neven if an inquiry into the complaint has begun.\n\nSchedule 2  Amendment of the Australian Human Rights Commission Act 1986\n\nHuman Rights Legislation Amendment Act 2017\n\nCompilation date: 01/09/2021\nRegistered: 03/11/2021\n\nMandatory termination of complaint\n\n(1B) The President must terminate a complaint if the President is\nsatisfied that:\n\n(a) the complaint is trivial, vexatious, misconceived or lacking in\nsubstance; or\n\n(b) there is no reasonable prospect of the matter being settled by\nconciliation.\n\n(1C) The President must terminate a complaint if the President is\nsatisfied that there would be no reasonable prospect that the\nFederal Court or the Federal Circuit Court would be satisfied that\nthe alleged acts, omissions or practices are unlawful\ndiscrimination.\n\n(1D) A complaint may be terminated under subsection (1B) or (1C) at\nany time, even if an inquiry into the complaint has begun.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017-sch-2-sec-43-ss-1a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017-sch-2-sec-43-ss-1b"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017-sch-2-sec-43-ss-1c"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017-sch-2-sec-43-ss-1d"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8445d5cfe714f4491bdd7be3a32948e53e2a96ef2d6d75ca8d501fbc73a359c4"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/human-rights-legislation-amendment-act-2017#sch-2-sec-43",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "43 After subsection 46PH(1)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 15,
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\n(1A) A complaint may be terminated under subsection (1) at any time,\neven if an inquiry into the complaint has begun.\n\nSchedule 2  Amendment of the Australian Human Rights Commission Act 1986\n\nHuman Rights Legislation Amendment Act 2017\n\nCompilation date: 01/09/2021\nRegistered: 03/11/2021\n\nMandatory termination of complaint\n\n(1B) The President must terminate a complaint if the President is\nsatisfied that:\n\n(a) the complaint is trivial, vexatious, misconceived or lacking in\nsubstance; or\n\n(b) there is no reasonable prospect of the matter being settled by\nconciliation.\n\n(1C) The President must terminate a complaint if the President is\nsatisfied that there would be no reasonable prospect that the\nFederal Court or the Federal Circuit Court would be satisfied that\nthe alleged acts, omissions or practices are unlawful\ndiscrimination.\n\n(1D) A complaint may be terminated under subsection (1B) or (1C) at\nany time, even if an inquiry into the complaint has begun."
    },
